**How to implement.** The constructor windows run the kit window: the kit bar over the workbench, the real shell, and the change check on every activation (001 §E 'on activation, files changed outside the app … are offered for reload'; the S5.3 brief: on window activation, run S4.1's external-change check; 001 §O: the title shows the kit name and folder). In `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `ConstructorScene.mount` (`Program.fs:71`), its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: (1) It runs `Program.mkProgram` instead of `Program.mkSimple`, capturing the Elmish dispatch from its init command as `LibraryWindow` does (`LibraryWindow.fs:90`): init answers `seed ()` with `kitShell = { explorer = ExplorerProxy.system; requestClose = window.Close }` (steps 183, 186) and `Cmd.ofEffect` storing the dispatch; update is `updateTableAndElementRotation` with `Cmd.none`. (2) Its view keeps setting `window.Title <- model.kitWindowTitle.value` (step 184) and answers `KitWindowView.kitWindowView model dispatch` (step 188) in place of `mainView`, so the kit bar shows above the workbench. (3) `window.Activated.Add (fun _ -> dispatch (CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnActivation))` (step 187), so every activation, the first included, checks the kit; the first finds nothing, because opening the kit recorded its stamps (step 131). `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` keep their constructors and their `Closed` release (step 154), and their docs say they run the kit window. No timer, file watcher or polling is added. Tests, in `KitWindowTests` (step 184), each over `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName "KitWindowTests")` and a kit from `TestAppScope.openedKitIn` (step 152), with trait `ui-smoke`: `acceptance: activating a constructor window offers the kit files changed outside the app, and Reload reads them in`: a shown `MainConstructorWindow` holds `kitBar` and no `kitChangesText`; another writer (`KitProxy.create` over the kit's folder, step 126) writes an experiment `E2` through `writeExperiment` (step 148), an experiment committed in a scratch `initMain ()` model and given `id = ExperimentId 2`; a second `Window` is shown and activated, then the constructor window is activated again (`Activate ()`), and `kitChangesText` names `E2.experiment-json`; pressing `kitChangesReloadButton` at its centre removes the offer, and, its Experiments tab pressed, the collection holds `E2`'s row. `Close kit closes the window and releases the kit`: pressing `kitCloseButton` closes the window (its `Closed` raised once), and the kit's folder holds no `.oc/lock`. Neither fact presses `kitShowInExplorerButton`, because a real window's explorer is the system's.

**Acceptance.** After the windows run the kit window, a constructor window MUST show the kit bar above the workbench, use the system explorer and its own close, and check its kit for outside changes on every activation; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: activating a constructor window offers the kit files changed outside the app, and Reload reads them in` and `Close kit closes the window and releases the kit`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.
